{"name":"Scott Base","hex":"#66a3c3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Scott Base","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A research station on Ross Island in Antarctica."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Scott_Base"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scott Base","blocks":[{"text":"Scott Base is a New Zealand Antarctic research station at Pram Point on Ross Island near Mount Erebus in New Zealand's Ross Dependency territorial claim. It was named in honour of Captain Robert Falcon Scott, RN, leader of two British expeditions to the Ross Sea area of Antarctica. The base was set up as support to field research and the centre for research into earth sciences, and now conducts research in many fields, operated by Antarctica New Zealand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Scott_Base_from_air.jpg/330px-Scott_Base_from_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Base"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Scott_Base%2C_Antarctica%2C_Jan_2006.jpg/500px-Scott_Base%2C_Antarctica%2C_Jan_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Scott_Base%2C_Antarctica%2C_Jan_2006.jpg/1280px-Scott_Base%2C_Antarctica%2C_Jan_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Scott_Base%2C_Antarctica%2C_Jan_2006.jpg/500px-Scott_Base%2C_Antarctica%2C_Jan_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial photograph of Scott Base, Ross Island, Antarctica","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScott_Base%2C_Antarctica%2C_Jan_2006.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Mcmurdo_oli_2013334.jpg/500px-Mcmurdo_oli_2013334.jpg?utm_source=en.wi